store_head raises head_generation_ only when the key directory's version
changes. A failed flush's head can take sequences that change no key, and
resume() gives them out again: an answer prepared there takes a later write
of that sequence for one it saw, and a write-write conflict is missed (#754).
Guarded-by: "prepared validation: a plan prepared in a head whose sequence resume() gives out again is checked again"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index 8a641099..25defdc2 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -1829,7 +1829,8 @@ private:
   void store_head(std::shared_ptr<EngineState> s) {
     const auto replaced = std::atomic_exchange(&head_, std::move(s));
     if (replaced == nullptr) return;  // the first head
-    head_generation_.fetch_add(1);
+    if (replaced->key_dir.version() != std::atomic_load(&head_)->key_dir.version())
+      head_generation_.fetch_add(1);
   }
 #pragma clang diagnostic pop
 
